# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

## Summary
Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React project by following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **Code/src/App.jsx**
  - Fixed incorrect import: Changed from `@vercel/analytics/vue` to `@vercel/analytics/react`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component to the JSX tree (placed at the end of the fragment for optimal placement)

## Implementation Details

### What Was Already Done:
- The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already installed in package.json

### What I Fixed:
The project had an incorrect Analytics configuration. The import statement was using the Vue version instead of the React version. I corrected this according to the official Vercel Analytics documentation for React/Vite projects.

### Changes:
1. **Corrected Import Statement**: Changed from `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/vue"` to `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react"`
2. **Rendered Analytics Component**: Added `<Analytics />` component to the JSX tree in the App component

### Why This Implementation:
- According to Vercel's quickstart documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), React/Vite projects should import from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- The Analytics component should be rendered once in the root component to track all page views
- Placed at the end of the fragment to ensure it doesn't interfere with the main app rendering

## Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Project builds successfully with no errors
✅ **Lint Test**: No new linting errors introduced in App.jsx
✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file updated (though no new packages were needed as @vercel/analytics was already installed)

## Next Steps for Deployment

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Navigate to Analytics in the Vercel dashboard
2. Click "Enable" if not already enabled
3. After deployment and user visits, analytics data will appear in the dashboard within a few days
4. Verify tracking by checking the browser Network tab for analytics requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Notes
- The project already had the Analytics package installed but was using the wrong import path
- No additional configuration files needed for this setup
- Analytics will automatically track page views across all routes defined in the React Router configuration
